    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d421">

                <pb facs="0753" n="683" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg683"/>

                <head>No. 420.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Romero.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-02-16"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 16,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 7th instant, in relation to the Apache Indians, who, it is
                    represented, have been leaving the San Carlos Reservation in Arizona Territory
                    and invading Sonora, Mexico.</p>
                <p>I have accordingly submitted copy of your note to the Secretaries of War and of
                    the Interior, who have been asked to adopt such further measures as may be found
                    practicable by their respective Departments for the suppression of the abuses
                    complained of.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
